# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/

# Tool caches
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.coverage

# Documentation build output (`make docs`). The sources under docs/ ARE tracked; only the
# rendered HTML and Sphinx's doctree cache are not.
docs/_build/

# Generated data, never source: the accumulated store, per-run candidate and validation
# output, and the analysis files built from them (`make calibration`, the benchmark log).
#
# Note the blanket *.csv and *.db: this repo deliberately commits NO candidate data at all.
# A committed slice of the store used to back `make demo`, and it shipped difficulty tiers,
# self-dock RMSDs and PLIP counts for candidates the course assigns as exercises -- the
# exercise's own answers. `scripts/demo_run.py` runs a real pipeline from zero instead, so
# there is nothing to commit and nothing to leak, and there is no exception to these rules.
# tests/protein_selector/test_no_committed_answers.py enforces that.
*.csv
*.parquet
*.db
cache/
results/

# Run logs
slurm/logs/

# Left over from the Snakemake era (removed 2026-08-29). Kept so an old working copy's
# leftovers stay out of `git status`; nothing writes here any more.
.snakemake/
